    "comments": "",
    "internalNotes": "John, Samantha, Isira,\n\nGraceview Adventist College brings 15 students on Friday 25 September, and this is not a River Day. They booked the goat and alpaca feeding at $5 a child, with the grounds open to them around it. There are no rotation blocks, no chosen sessions and no horse work. Staff it for one: one person runs the feeding and meets the coach. They have paid in full, so there is nothing to collect on the day.\n\nThe booking, from Rezdy\n\nOrder\tR11RTL1\nSchool\tGraceview Adventist College, Reedy Creek\nContact\tCharlie Barnett, Teacher Aide, 0436 378 790, charlie.barnett@graceview.qld.edu.au\nDate\tFriday 25 September 2026\nCoach\tThe school says 10am. Be set from 09:45 and hold until they arrive. I will confirm the window with Charlie Barnett and tell you if it moves.\nGroup\t15 students, Prep to Year 6\nTheir supervision\tTheir own staff at 1:10\nBooked and paid\tGoat and Alpaca Feeding Experience, 15 at $5, $75 paid by EFT on 3 September\nDietary, medical or access needs\tNone declared at booking\nWhat they were promised in writing, on 11 August\n\nThe feeding at the $75 Isira approved, and around it the grounds at no charge: the riverside walk down to the turtle jetty, the mill museum, and the lawns for lunch. If children bring pocket money, the ice creams and the gift shop are open to them. Nothing else was included. If they ask for anything that carries a price, send it to the office; it is not agreed at the gate.\n\nBefore they arrive\n\nHave the feed made up for 15 children. Set the handwashing station at the exit of the animal area, with soap and paper towel, and check the sanitiser pumps. Clear the coach drop-off near the main gates. Have the toilets checked and open. They eat on the lawns or at the picnic tables, and they bring their own food.\n\nWhen the coach pulls in\n\nGreet the driver and the lead teacher. Ask the teacher then and there whether any child has an allergy, a medical need or an access need, because the booking field was left blank three weeks ago. Toilets first. Then read the safety read-out aloud to the children and the adults together, and have the lead teacher sign it. Read it even though the visit is short: it is what puts supervision and duty of care in writing with their staff. Photograph the signed page and send it to admin@rivermill.au, so the record sits with the booking.\n\nThe feeding\n\nRun it as the standard goat and alpaca feeding. Feed only from the buckets we provide, flat hand, gentle and calm. With 15 children it is one group, not a rotation. The tour script gives you talking points for the goats, the sheep and the alpacas, and for the turtles at the jetty if you walk down with them. Prep to Year 6 is a wide span in one group, so pitch it to the age in front of you. Handwashing with soap and water straight after the animals, and again before they eat.\n\nThe rest of their day\n\nThey walk the grounds themselves. Their teachers keep supervision throughout at their own 1:10, including on the river walk and at the jetty. Everyone stays behind the rail and nobody goes in the water. The museum is open to them. If it rains, the museum and the pavilion are the cover.\n\nHorses are not part of this booking. No grooming and no rides. If the children ask, the answer is that the horses are not part of today.\n\nFirst aid stays with their school for the students, including any medicines. Our first-aid kit and the defibrillator are in the Caf\u00e9 building, and our staff can call 000.\n\nDeparture is the lead teacher&#039;s headcount, then loading. If anything goes wrong, or the teacher raises something, call the office on (07) 3703 1307 and I will follow it up with the school.\n\nAttached, everything this booking needs. The safety read-out to read aloud and have signed. The tour script for the talking points. The terms and conditions the booking sits under. The venue risk assessment, which is also the copy the school holds. And E60, our full onsite procedure for school groups. E60 is written for the full River Day, so treat its rotation timetable as background rather than as the plan for 25 September.\n\nPriyanka",
